eld/choices "answer-bace1e39-b96c-5598-91da-f2e30385e626"] ["answer-field-20ae3d0b-c166-52e0-b469-1972d9f84ee6" :answer-field/choices "answer-e526436b-9a51-5f65-a668-0eb96ca49eb0"] ["question-b91cf75b-843d-5d15-ac06-6485f918c5af" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-20ae3d0b-c166-52e0-b469-1972d9f84ee6"] [17592186198279 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b91cf75b-843d-5d15-ac06-6485f918c5af"] [17592186198700 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/id #uuid "63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c"] ["question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/math-academy-id "q-174455"] ["question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/problem "Find the truth set of the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\ge -1$\n\nwhere the universal set is $N.$"] ["question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P(x)$ is the set of elements in its universal set $U$ such that substituting these elements for the variable makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{x\\in U\\,|\\,P(x)\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U=N.$\n\nWe need to find $x\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}\\ge -1$\n\nWe know that the square of any real number is greater than or equal to zero.\n\nSo, the inequality is true for every real number. In particular, it's true for every $x\\in N.$ \n\nTherefore, the truth set of our predicate is $T=N.$"] ["question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/id #uuid "c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61"] ["answer-2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6" :answer/id #uuid "2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6"] ["answer-2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6" :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" :answer/id #uuid "28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29"] ["answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29" :answer/value "N"] ["answer-49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66" :answer/id #uuid "49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66"] ["answer-49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66" :answer/value "[-1,\\infty )"] ["answer-2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf" :answer/id #uuid "2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf"] ["answer-2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf" :answer/value "[0,\\infty )"] ["answer-caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5" :answer/id #uuid "caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5"] ["answer-caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5" :answer/value "∅"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/correct "answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/choices "answer-2fa96fcc-d445-5126-bab7-2fc1e9c246b6"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/choices "answer-28bc466a-f300-5f57-aec7-9770f3d2ff29"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/choices "answer-49b6b7fb-0b48-59e8-9257-b19da9baea66"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/choices "answer-2849368e-65ae-57ea-a549-07c4abeb0fbf"] ["answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61" :answer-field/choices "answer-caf2dff0-9187-5e23-869d-71431326dff5"] ["question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c66a38f3-27df-56d2-bf7d-219d907e9d61"] [17592186198279 :knowledge-point/questions "question-63a5ac6a-aab7-51ca-954b-e590d679441c"] ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/id #uuid "9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e"] ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/math-academy-id "q-175354"] ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $8$ divided by $t.$\n\nII. $y$ multiplied by $z.$\n\nIII. $p$ is a composite number."] ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $t$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(y,z)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $p$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""] ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa"] ["answer-e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953" :answer/id #uuid "e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953"] ["answer-e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c" :answer/id #uuid "f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c"] ["answer-f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466" :answer/id #uuid "6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466"] ["answer-6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef" :answer/id #uuid "e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef"] ["answer-e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644" :answer/id #uuid "503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644"] ["answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/correct "answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/choices "answer-e6487afd-7bcc-5095-afa4-646349f2e953"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/choices "answer-f9fee152-d57a-5195-85ee-6823b5351b2c"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/choices "answer-6b6d8060-0176-5175-aa8f-1706ba311466"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/choices "answer-e08b2963-8bca-50ae-82c1-0c92043cecef"] ["answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa" :answer-field/choices "answer-503d8faa-f079-5132-ade3-e4f9cc774644"] ["question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9d057fd8-1279-514e-b87c-868f979ed1fa"] [17592186198280 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9d2ae0ef-2e2b-52c8-a273-c086772b799e"] ["question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/id #uuid "b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d"] ["question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/math-academy-id "q-175352"] ["question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nI. $q$ plus $3.$\n\nII. $2$ is greater than $x.$\n\nIII. $a$ is a divisor of $b.$"] ["question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $q$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(a,b)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] ["question-b5cdaff3-81ba-58ae-a27f-1dea94cd990d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b08c9d99-93d0-59db-a882-7330c0dcbd51" :answer-field/id #uuid "b08c9d99-93d0-59db-a882-7330c0dcbd51"] ["answer-9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5" :answer/id #uuid "9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5"] ["answer-9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-9ce84ceb-40f0-55b4-a8f2-42694ec7bec5" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-7ebde441-31ee-5c72-be00-ba395690a42b" :answe