-field-32567726-3501-5d0d-940f-48d231eb6ef4"] [17592186198280 :knowledge-point/questions "question-29e9adcf-4a5b-51ac-835b-f4a444c16f67"] ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/id #uuid "ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d"] ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/math-academy-id "q-174401"] ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?"] ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4$\n\nLet's first rearrange our inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{4}<1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that this represents an ellipse centered at $O$ with semi-axes $2$ and $1.$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/fd/fdb0a299dd6ee0bd58ceb1a74c9423bf5cac81857b0538dcda7f0a4cba9a1108.png)"] ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f"] ["answer-1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7" :answer/id #uuid "1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7"] ["answer-1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7" :answer/value "images/14/14031d9643e2bb32ad00e8f715e62399b68a970ba56f0aede4d718ad187084d6.png"] ["answer-adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945" :answer/id #uuid "adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945"] ["answer-adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945" :answer/value "images/17/178f6746c8a9984f163b398317da9c5b40fa84331a5643625e63fcb1439c9d0c.png"] ["answer-a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83" :answer/id #uuid "a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83"] ["answer-a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83" :answer/value "images/c0/c058c940715b7a2a4a844a360d88cda3daa6455eed159fbee0dfb7545ddbf1a6.png"] ["answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" :answer/id #uuid "9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4"] ["answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4" :answer/value "images/fd/fdb0a299dd6ee0bd58ceb1a74c9423bf5cac81857b0538dcda7f0a4cba9a1108.png"] ["answer-c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17" :answer/id #uuid "c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17"] ["answer-c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17" :answer/value "images/fe/fef6b4ac68f92490c510e0570968e0f2efbe92de0ec60b1eb4c99545a2713259.png"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/correct "answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/choices "answer-1bd102d7-98fa-5661-bd09-9693e3c677d7"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/choices "answer-adc9353f-873d-5ce4-8975-2cb89b75f945"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/choices "answer-a3b91979-e90f-57f4-8242-78efe6079f83"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/choices "answer-9f8f7227-b926-5556-bd09-6a48c3ee78d4"] ["answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f" :answer-field/choices "answer-c345dc13-6285-512f-95b1-d0d4a4223f17"] ["question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f0f7f6bf-8e15-5716-bb8d-0bc39135a77f"] [17592186198281 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ca53c000-4fe4-56e9-a6ee-1afd2eed227d"] ["question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/id #uuid "78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad"] ["question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-175387"] ["question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/problem "Consider the following predicate:\n\n$\\,$ $P(x,y):$ $x+y<3,$\n\nwhere the universal set is ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded regions represents the truth set of the predicate?"] ["question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/worked-solution "The *truth set* of a predicate $P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})$ is the set of $n$-tuples in its universal set $U={U}_{1}\\times {U}_{2}\\times ⋯\\times {U}_{n}$ such that substituting these tuples for the variables makes the predicate a true statement:\n\n$$\nT=\\{({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\in U\\,|\\,P({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\}\n$$\n\nThe universal set for our predicate is $U={R}^{2}.$\n\nWe need to find $(x,y)\\in U$ such that the following is true:\n\n$\\,$ $x+y<3$\n\nNow, we convert the inequality into the slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & <3 \\\\ y & <-x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's sketch the truth set $T$ of $P(x,y):$\n\n![](images/bd/bde3d6ee1e58d33088ffc49913e1cd8a299f0ea91cdf4024fd0b63a598ebf456.png)"] ["question-78dba0d1-f872-5b82-8f2b-f5d37f8cf2ad" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b0ca923a-2a7a-5fd9-9f3d